From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] touch: hold the screen 10 s to recalibrate

The touch screen is the AD5X's only input. When the touch calibration
does not fit the panel, the screen that fixes it cannot be reached from
the screen: it takes SSH (HELIX_TOUCH_CALIBRATE=1, --calibrate-touch)
or editing settings.json (issue #90). The calibration screen itself
reads raw values, so only getting to it needs a gesture that does not
depend on where the finger lands.

A press held 10 s anywhere opens touch calibration, the same overlay as
Settings, on any screen, the wizard included. It is timed in
calibrated_read_cb on the raw press state, before LVGL hands the press
to a widget:

- releases shorter than 200 ms inside the hold are digitizer noise
- when it fires, the widget under the finger gets PRESS_LOST (a jog
  pad stops its hold repeat) and LVGL waits for the release, so the
  release is not a click
- it fires once per press and is armed again only after 3 s with no
  touch, so a panel that reports a touch all the time does not open
  calibration over and over
- nothing happens while calibration is already open

Signed-off-by: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
---
 include/touch_calibration_wrapper.h           | 18 ++++++
 src/application/application.cpp               | 22 +++++++
 src/application/application_shutdown.cpp      |  2 +
 .../input/touch_calibration_wrapper.cpp       | 60 +++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 102 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/touch_calibration_wrapper.h b/include/touch_calibration_wrapper.h
index 55687ea50e..084be55958 100644
--- a/include/touch_calibration_wrapper.h
+++ b/include/touch_calibration_wrapper.h
@@ -85,6 +85,24 @@ struct CalibrationContext {
 /// samples within one press.
 inline constexpr int kTransposedGuessCorroboration = 3;
 
+/// A press held this long anywhere on the screen opens touch calibration
+/// (set_calibration_hold_handler). It is measured on the raw press state, before
+/// LVGL hands the press to a widget, so it works with any calibration.
+inline constexpr uint32_t kCalibrationHoldMs = 10000;
+/// A release shorter than this inside a hold is digitizer noise, not a lift.
+inline constexpr uint32_t kCalibrationHoldGapMs = 200;
+/// After the hold fires, it is armed again only once the panel has reported no
+/// touch for this long, so a panel that reports a touch all the time does not
+/// open calibration over and over.
+inline constexpr uint32_t kCalibrationHoldRearmMs = 3000;
+
+/// Called on the LVGL thread, from the read callback, when a press has been held
+/// for kCalibrationHoldMs. Returns true when it takes the hold (and schedules the
+/// calibration screen); the press is then ended so the widget under the finger
+/// gets no click. Returns false to leave the press alone (calibration already
+/// open). nullptr turns the gesture off.
+void set_calibration_hold_handler(std::function<bool()> handler);
+
 /// Read callback wrapper that applies affine touch calibration.
 /// Chains to original_read_cb first, then transforms coordinates.
 void calibrated_read_cb(lv_indev_t* indev, lv_indev_data_t* data);
